# Line endings.
#
# The repository is stored with LF and every checkout keeps LF, on every
# platform. Without this, a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF in the
# working tree while `cargo xtask gen-readme-diagrams` writes LF, so a
# regenerated diagram would show a whole-file diff that is not a change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated or binary assets: never line-ending-translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.tar.gz binary

# The diagrams are generated text; keep them diffable and LF.
docs/images/*.svg text eol=lf

# Test fixtures that must stay byte-exact.
*.ref text eol=lf
*.manifest text eol=lf

# GitHub Linguist — the repository is Rust, and only Rust.
#
# The tooling, the crates and the build are Rust; nothing else here is a
# programming language Linguist should count. The Refal corpus (`.ref`) is the
# artifact the compiler is tested *against*, not a host language of this
# repository, and it has no Linguist language of its own; the Markdown is
# documentation; and the SVG diagram family is generated. Pinned explicitly so
# the language bar is a property of this file rather than of Linguist's
# heuristics — which is what stops a future asset from silently re-entering the
# breakdown the way the removed `scripts/*.py` and `*.sh` once did.
*.ref linguist-documentation
*.md linguist-documentation
*.manifest linguist-documentation
docs/images/*.svg linguist-generated linguist-documentation
